From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:49:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pool): an Anthropic credits_required 429 benches the
 model until the weekly reset [daveey]

Fable has its own allowance per Claude Max account. When it is spent, Anthropic
answers 429 'Usage credits are required for this model' with
details.error_code=credits_required and no usable reset, so the pool's one-hour
default bench applied. In an example incident the available accounts were out of Fable; a pinned
chat said 'out until the displayed reset' and the pool kept retrying an account that had no
Fable until its weekly window reopened.

extract_api_error_context now keeps details.error_code, and a credits_required
model cooldown lasts until the account's weekly reset from the usage cache,
never shorter than the error's own reset. No snapshot: unchanged behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
